## Delivered behavior

`LocalRoleRequestFactoryV5` now reloads each checkpoint-authorized projection record and emits exactly one aggregate evaluator evidence item, `failure.rendering.policy_source_unbounded_or_stateful_count`, only for a nonzero count of prior-round committed invalid records carrying the closed reserved failure code. Checkpoint equality, record reload equality, discovery-plan, PIT-scope, and semantic-mode checks are mandatory; load failures propagate. The item appears after all existing episode evidence and before archive/history evidence. The approved A allowlist and episode block are byte-identical to their preimage.

`OptimizerSummaryV5` now exposes defaulted `completed_lifecycle_rounds`, `evaluated_feedback_rounds`, and `render_rejected_experiments`. They preserve positional construction, use strict existing integer validation plus the specified consistency guard, and derive only after record authentication and `verify_projection`. Existing status/readiness/performance, tokens/costs, cleanup semantics, durable schemas, runtime/finalizer, and history/novelty behavior are unchanged.

